# Build-context exclusions for `podman build -f image/Containerfile .` (podman and
# buildah read .containerignore from the context root). Syntax as .dockerignore:
# patterns are relative to the context root, `**` matches any number of directories
# and a trailing `/` is ignored.
#
# image/Containerfile reads only these context paths, and nothing below may match them:
#   rpms/                         COPY (the local Apex repository)
#   image/system_files/           COPY (rootfs overlay)
#   image/, image/packages/       bind mounts (lists, checks, audit)
#   hardware/m7400qc/generated/   bind mount (rendered hardware files)

# Version control metadata.
.git/

# Cargo build output (many GiB).
target/

# Local work directories of .github/scripts (image.sh, qualify.sh) and VM disk images,
# which run to tens of GiB.
_build/
out/
**/*.qcow2
**/*.raw
**/*.iso

# Private keys: `cosign generate-key-pair` writes cosign.key next to cosign.pub. Keep
# them out of the build context even if one is left in the tree (secrets.sh would then
# fail the build on the key it finds in the image).
**/cosign.key
**/*.key

# Biometric data (as in .gitignore): a gitignored capture left in the tree, for example
# under hardware/m7400qc/generated or image/system_files, never reaches an image.
**/*.[Pp][Gg][Mm]
**/*.[Vv][Aa][Rr][Ii][Aa][Nn][Tt]
**/*.[Ii][Oo][Cc][Tt][Ll]
**/*.[Uu][Mm][Oo][Cc][Kk][Dd][Ee][Vv]
**/*.[Pp][Cc][Aa][Pp]
**/*.[Pp][Cc][Aa][Pp][Nn][Gg]
**/var/lib/fprint/

# Tool caches.
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
